 no cheap downside or upside strike to pick out.\n- **Trend:** The yearly IV history rises slowly, from 24% in 2024 to 26% in 2025 and 27% in 2026. That series has only three points, so it tells me little about the trend.\n\nWhether to add depends on your view of the business, not on the option price. Two things from other nodes' documents point to risk. Pellham Power is 35% of utility orders, and it withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering and scaled back procurement. Utilities are 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026. Those risks aren't reflected in a 27% IV, which is only slightly above normal.\n\nI only checked IV level, skew and history. I didn't look at the actual option prices, strikes, expiries or theta cost.\n\nSources: the VLTX LEAPS pricing snapshot (`vltx-leaps`), the `vltx_iv_history` series, and the customer-mix document (`vltx-order-mix`).","ttft_ms":2327,"type":"result","duration_ms":19963,"uuid":"15855154-5331-4c64-85fd-1b5b36b08805","ttft_stream_ms":1555,"time_to_request_ms":290,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":74,"system_prompt":26,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":38,"input_hooks":10,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":10,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":23,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":7,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":7,"request_announcements":25,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":7,"client_creation":7,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":96,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":81,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":208,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":133,"process_rss_mib_result":199,"process_anon_mib_result":118,"process_peak_rss_mib":208,"process_cpu_ms_turn":532,"process_wall_ms_turn":19953,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":59,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1362,"main_